abstract: >-
  An evidence-driven Quality Engineering framework for security testing AI
  agents across prompt injection, tool abuse, excessive agency, identity and
  authorization, scope escalation, data leakage, tenant isolation, memory and
  tool poisoning, human approval, repeated side effects, resource abuse,
  observability, adversarial discovery, permanent security regression and CI/CD
  release gates. The work emphasizes that agent reasoning may propose actions,
  but authoritative identity, authorization, deterministic policy, least
  privilege and human control must constrain execution.